// glm-pipe repro: the classic diverging-loop idiom is rejected by the
// semantic validator with MISSING_RETURN. `_returns_on_all_paths` returns
// False for WHILE/FOR, even when the condition is the literal `true` and
// the body returns. The type checker explicitly documents infinite loops
// as non-errors (a7/passes/type_checker.py:617-621), so the two passes
// disagree.
spin :: fn() i32 {
    while true {
        ret 1
    }
}
